@AdrianLxM I know the format more or less, and yes it could be mixed. All what needs to be done is to name the right fields in the header. Nevertheless I can request the data structure, if I have problems, from the SiDiary-Team ;) 
May also a interface could be possible, to transfer the data via gmail to Sidiary-online, to let import it there in the background (used that in the past for Glimp-Data). But this should be the next step what I have in mind.

I'm not sure if it will be the best to separate the files by datatype. May it could be interested to made settings available which kind of data should be included in the export-File? We will see. At first I will try to implement just the rough Export all in one, just to check that everything comes in a way that the data could be well imported. After that we can see how to increase the export ;)

Does it import correctly if treatments and BG values are not set in ascending order?

Maybe it helps to add the timezone to the formatter:
``` 
df.setTimeZone(TimeZone.getDefault());
java.text.DateFormat df = new SimpleDateFormat("dd.MM.yyyy;HH:mm;");
```
